{"step_index":236,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T18:03:58Z","thinking":"**Confirming Initialization**\n\nI've confirmed that the `nexlev` server is properly listed within `mcp_config.json`. My next observation is that Antigravity, upon starting, attempts to execute `npx -y mcp-remote https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp` to initialize the MCP server in the background. This seems like a promising initial setup.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Disable NexLev MCP auto-start to prevent annoying auth popups on IDE launch.\"","EndLine":"42","Instruction":"\"Disable the nexlev server in mcp_config.json\"","ReplacementContent":"\"    \\\"nexlev\\\": {\\n      \\\"disabled\\\": true,\\n      \\\"command\\\": \\\"npx\\\",\\n      \\\"args\\\": [\\n        \\\"-y\\\",\\n        \\\"mcp-remote\\\",\\n        \\\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\"","StartLine":"35","TargetContent":"\"    \\\"nexlev\\\": {\\n      \\\"command\\\": \\\"npx\\\",\\n      \\\"args\\\": [\\n        \\\"-y\\\",\\n        \\\"mcp-remote\\\",\\n        \\\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\"","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\config\\\\mcp_config.json\"","toolAction":"\"Disabling NexLev auto-start\"","toolSummary":"\"Disable NexLev in mcp_config\""}}]}
