{"step_index":238,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T18:04:11Z","content":"I know exactly why this is happening and I just fixed it for you!\n\n**Why it was happening:**\nAntigravity automatically tries to connect to all configured tools in the background every time you open it. Because NexLev's `mcp-remote` tool uses an OAuth flow, Antigravity checking it in the background was triggering that browser popup over and over again on startup.\n\n**How I solved it:**\nI went into your `mcp_config.json` file and set `\"disabled\": true` for NexLev. \n\nThis tells Antigravity to **stop** trying to connect to it on startup. You will no longer get that annoying popup when you open the IDE.\n\n**Can we still use NexLev?**\nYes! Because earlier we built the `nexlev-mcp-caller` custom skill with our own Python scripts, we bypass the built-in system entirely. The popup is gone, but anytime you ask me to \"check a channel using NexLev\", my custom script will run and pull the data perfectly.\n\nYou might need to restart Antigravity one last time for the config change to take effect, but you shouldn't see that popup anymore!"}
